  "question": {
    "text": "In a Young&#39;s double slit experiment, slits are separated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>, and the screen is placed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> away. A beam of light consisting of two wavelengths, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>650</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>520</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>, is used to obtain interference fringes on the screen. The least distance from the common central maximum to the point where the bright fringes due to both the wavelengths coincide is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tDoCJ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YgS9v",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QnQVX",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "wNuU0",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
